  "interpretation": [
    "The initial O2 proof-on slowdown is preserved but was not reproduced in the five-process alternating follow-up.",
    "Both O2 variants have identical measured kernel and timer-envelope machine code; retained hot checks, different inlining, or different loop instruction selection cannot explain a proof-on-only slowdown here.",
    "The inner16-element recurrence is unrolled identically at O2; vector copies in main transfer the returned array, not SIMD arithmetic.",
    "O0 has fewer emitted guards and a smaller code section with proof; the local pooled median decreases, but causal timing decomposition and universal speedups are not established.",
    "No affinity, frequency, thermal, or scheduling trace establishes an OS-level cause for the initial difference."
